  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Cornusalterin F may interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a series of intermediate targets. Specifically, Cornusalterin F is predicted to target an EDD domain protein from the DegV family, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Androstanedione and RA-Xii. These compounds are also predicted to target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The varying scores across the paths indicate a degree of confidence in the predicted interactions, with the highest score (0.6309) for the path involving Androstanedione and the second-highest score (0.5947) for the path involving RA-Xii. The presence of multiple pathways converging on UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 suggests a potential mechanism involving the EDD domain protein as a common intermediary. The evidence supports the hypothesis that Cornusalterin F may modulate UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through the DegV family protein, though the exact nature of the interaction and the role of the intermediate compounds remains to be fully elucidated.",
